","DOI":"10.1021/acs.jmedchem.4c01026","Year":2024,"Counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","Type":"IC50"},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-023401","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"3a","Cell_line":"HL-7702 (L-02)","Time(h)":48,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":">200","IC50_Dark_value":200,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1021/acs.jmedchem.4c01026","Year":2024,"Counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","Type":"IC50"}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"3a","value":1.83,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","temperature_C":27,"doi":"10.1021/acs.jmedchem.4c01026","year":2024,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-003734","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipid-water partition coefficients of the complexes 3a-3c were determined by shake flash method. The standard curve was firstly obtained by preparing three complexes with different concentration gradients using water saturated octanol solution. Subsequently, 1 mg of the complexes added to a mixture of 1 mL water and1 mL octanol. Then the mixture was shaken in a thermostatic shaker (150 rpm/min and 300 K) for 24 h. Centrifugation at 1000 rpm for 5 min was allowed to stand pending separation of the upper and lower layers. UV-Vis spectra was used to determine the concentration of the complex in the organic phase (Co), the concentration of the complex in the H2O phase Cw = Ctotal–Co, finally the logP = log(Co/Cw) value was obtained."}]}